1. Coffee Machine consists of Water Tank, Coffee Bean Container, Milk Tank, Cup, Grinder, Heater, Brewing Unit, and Control Panel.

2. Water Tank can be empty or full.
3. Coffee Bean Container can be empty or full.
4. Milk Tank can be empty or full.
5. Cup can be empty or filled.

6. Coffee Type can be Espresso, Americano, Cappuccino, Latte, or Black Coffee.

7. Brewing Unit can be idle or brewing.
8. Grinder can be idle or grinding.
9. Heater can be off or heating.

10. User is the agent of Coffee Preparation.
11. User is the agent of Water Refill.
12. User is the agent of Bean Refill.
13. User is the agent of Milk Refill.
14. User is the agent of Coffee Selection.

15. Water Tank is an instrument of Coffee Preparation.
16. Coffee Bean Container is an instrument of Coffee Preparation.
17. Grinder is an instrument of Coffee Preparation.
18. Heater is an instrument of Coffee Preparation.
19. Brewing Unit is an instrument of Coffee Preparation.
20. Milk Tank is an instrument of Milk Frothing.

21. Coffee Selection requires User.
22. Coffee Selection yields Coffee Type.

23. Water Refill changes Water Tank from empty to full.
24. Water Refill requires Water Tank to be empty.

25. Bean Refill changes Coffee Bean Container from empty to full.
26. Bean Refill requires Coffee Bean Container to be empty.

27. Milk Refill changes Milk Tank from empty to full.
28. Milk Refill requires Milk Tank to be empty.

29. Grinding Coffee is a process.
30. User is the agent of Grinding Coffee.
31. Grinder is an instrument of Grinding Coffee.
32. Grinding Coffee consumes Coffee Beans.
33. Grinding Coffee yields Ground Coffee.

34. Heating Water is a process.
35. Heater is an instrument of Heating Water.
36. Heating Water requires Water Tank to be full.
37. Heating Water yields Hot Water.

38. Brewing Espresso is a process.
39. Brewing Unit is an instrument of Brewing Espresso.
40. Brewing Espresso requires Ground Coffee.
41. Brewing Espresso requires Hot Water.
42. Brewing Espresso changes Cup from empty to filled.
43. Brewing Espresso consumes Ground Coffee.
44. Brewing Espresso consumes Hot Water.

45. Brewing Americano is a process.
46. Brewing Americano requires Brewing Espresso.
47. Brewing Americano requires additional Hot Water.
48. Brewing Americano changes Cup from empty to filled.

49. Milk Frothing is a process.
50. Milk Tank is an instrument of Milk Frothing.
51. Milk Frothing consumes Milk.
52. Milk Frothing yields Frothed Milk.

53. Brewing Cappuccino is a process.
54. Brewing Cappuccino requires Brewing Espresso.
55. Brewing Cappuccino requires Milk Frothing.
56. Brewing Cappuccino changes Cup from empty to filled.
57. Brewing Cappuccino consumes Frothed Milk.

58. Brewing Latte is a process.
59. Brewing Latte requires Brewing Espresso.
60. Brewing Latte requires Milk Frothing.
61. Brewing Latte changes Cup from empty to filled.
62. Brewing Latte consumes Frothed Milk.

63. Brewing Black Coffee is a process.
64. Brewing Black Coffee requires Ground Coffee.
65. Brewing Black Coffee requires Hot Water.
66. Brewing Black Coffee changes Cup from empty to filled.

67. Coffee Preparation is a process.
68. User is the agent of Coffee Preparation.
69. Coffee Preparation requires Coffee Selection.
70. Coffee Preparation requires Water Tank to be full.
71. Coffee Preparation requires Coffee Bean Container to be full.

72. Coffee Preparation consumes Water.
73. Coffee Preparation consumes Coffee Beans.

74. Coffee Preparation invokes Grinding Coffee.
75. Coffee Preparation invokes Heating Water.

76. Coffee Preparation invokes Brewing Espresso if Coffee Type is Espresso.
77. Coffee Preparation invokes Brewing Americano if Coffee Type is Americano.
78. Coffee Preparation invokes Brewing Cappuccino if Coffee Type is Cappuccino.
79. Coffee Preparation invokes Brewing Latte if Coffee Type is Latte.
80. Coffee Preparation invokes Brewing Black Coffee if Coffee Type is Black Coffee.

81. Coffee Preparation yields Filled Cup.

82. Cleaning Machine is a process.
83. User is the agent of Cleaning Machine.
84. Cleaning Machine requires Coffee Machine.
85. Cleaning Machine changes Coffee Machine from dirty to clean.

86. Coffee Machine can be ready, preparing, or maintenance.
87. Coffee Preparation changes Coffee Machine from ready to preparing.
88. Coffee Preparation changes Coffee Machine from preparing to ready.
89. Cleaning Machine changes Coffee Machine from maintenance to ready.